# The figure working set. Whether you ignore these is a real decision, not a default —
# see the note at the top of test/golden.test.mjs and the last section of DOCTRINE.md.
#
# Ignoring them (the PSV choice): only the published PNG is committed, the golden suite
# only protects a tree that already has the sources locally, and re-deriving a figure is a
# RE-SHOOT rather than a re-render. That is survivable only if every figure has a prose
# page recording how to get back to it.
#
# Committing them: figures become re-renderable by anyone, the goldens work on a fresh
# clone, and you pay the repo size of every raw capture. If you have the room, do this.
#
# Uncomment to ignore:
# figures/sources/
# figures/*.json

# The demo's golden IS committed, so `npm test` verifies a fresh install end to end.
# test/golden/
